\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The drainhole ($\eta _0=2$, $\gamma =-\pi $) and symmetric ($\eta _0=1$, $\gamma =0$) families across the spin range, against $v_e$: (a) mass, angular momentum and equatorial throat radius; (b) $J/M^2$ against the Kerr bound; (c) the ratio of end masses; (d) the flattening $R_p/R_e$; (e) the exotic matter, the phantom field's integrated null-energy violation $\mathcal  {I}=\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ (\rho +p_\eta )\,dV$ over the $t=\,$const slice~\cite  {visser2003}, per equatorial throat radius, with the 3D runs (squares) placed by the scalar charge measured on each run's own $t=0$ slice, which reproduces its background's to $3\times 10^{-4}$; (f) the throat angular velocity, which peaks and falls to zero at extremality. The symmetric family violates the Kerr bound at every spin and the drainhole family exceeds it by up to $\sim 20\%$ at intermediate spin; the exotic matter per throat radius falls a hundredfold along the drainhole family and tenfold along the symmetric one by $v_e=0.99$; both families end on extremal Kerr.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trends}{{3}{5}{The drainhole ($\eta _0=2$, $\gamma =-\pi $) and symmetric ($\eta _0=1$, $\gamma =0$) families across the spin range, against $v_e$: (a) mass, angular momentum and equatorial throat radius; (b) $J/M^2$ against the Kerr bound; (c) the ratio of end masses; (d) the flattening $R_p/R_e$; (e) the exotic matter, the phantom field's integrated null-energy violation $\mathcal {I}=\int (\rho +p_\eta )\,dV$ over the $t=\,$const slice~\cite {visser2003}, per equatorial throat radius, with the 3D runs (squares) placed by the scalar charge measured on each run's own $t=0$ slice, which reproduces its background's to $3\times 10^{-4}$; (f) the throat angular velocity, which peaks and falls to zero at extremality. The symmetric family violates the Kerr bound at every spin and the drainhole family exceeds it by up to $\sim 20\%$ at intermediate spin; the exotic matter per throat radius falls a hundredfold along the drainhole family and tenfold along the symmetric one by $v_e=0.99$; both families end on extremal Kerr}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces The two families at representative spins, in units of $\eta _0$: rotation velocity $v_e$, angular momentum, mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end, ratio of end masses, scalar charge, equatorial throat radius, flattening, and throat angular velocity---each read off the solution's functions as defined in Sec.~\ref {sec:model}. Every row is a converged solution that passed the acceptance gates of Sec.~\ref {sec:solver}.}}{5}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:backgrounds}{{II}{5}{The two families at representative spins, in units of $\eta _0$: rotation velocity $v_e$, angular momentum, mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end, ratio of end masses, scalar charge, equatorial throat radius, flattening, and throat angular velocity---each read off the solution's functions as defined in Sec.~\ref {sec:model}. Every row is a converged solution that passed the acceptance gates of Sec.~\ref {sec:solver}}{table.2}{}}
