\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces The runs: the drainhole family (a) along the ladder, in code units. $8\pi J/A$ is the angular momentum in per cent of its extremal bound and $M_{\rm  ADM}$ the mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end (both from the background tables). The finest $\Delta x$ is $0.0625$ at $N=128$ on $L=64$ and at $N=256$ on $L=128$, and scales inversely with $N$ within a triplet. Recipe S (slow): $\sigma =0.1$, $\chi \ge 10^{-8}$; F (fast): $\sigma =0.4$, $\chi \ge 10^{-4}$. Shell: the damping layer of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:boundary} on ($\text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}$) or the background-relative boundary alone (--). Trust: the last time the run is quoted. GW: the $(2,0)$ burst at $R=14$ inside the trust window ($\text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}$), only its onset (the signal still rising at the window's end), or nothing above the extraction floor (--). The last three rows are in flight at this draft.}}{6}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ladder}{{III}{6}{The runs: the drainhole family (a) along the ladder, in code units. $8\pi J/A$ is the angular momentum in per cent of its extremal bound and $M_{\rm ADM}$ the mass of the $\eta \to +\infty $ end (both from the background tables). The finest $\Delta x$ is $0.0625$ at $N=128$ on $L=64$ and at $N=256$ on $L=128$, and scales inversely with $N$ within a triplet. Recipe S (slow): $\sigma =0.1$, $\chi \ge 10^{-8}$; F (fast): $\sigma =0.4$, $\chi \ge 10^{-4}$. Shell: the damping layer of Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:boundary} on ($\checkmark $) or the background-relative boundary alone (--). Trust: the last time the run is quoted. GW: the $(2,0)$ burst at $R=14$ inside the trust window ($\checkmark $), only its onset (the signal still rising at the window's end), or nothing above the extraction floor (--). The last three rows are in flight at this draft}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces One rate, two fates: the measured rate $1/\tau $ (left axis; $\tau $ right) against the angular momentum as a fraction of its extremal bound. Filled circles: collapsing rungs, $\tau $ from the log-linear fit of the areal-radius deficit over the 0.2--1\% band. Filled triangles: inflating rungs, $\tau $ from $\ln |dR_A/dt|$ over the $+0.2$--1\% growth band (the same fit on a pure exponential). Open circle: the stable 0.9c. Dashed: the fit $a-b\,(J/A)^2$ through both branches, which reaches zero at $42\%$. Open diamonds: the second-order rates of Refs.~\cite  {azad2023,azad2024} at $C=1$; dotted rules: their conjectured end of the instability (${\approx }30\%$) and the zero of their second-order rate ($33\%$). The outcome: the mode slows with spin, changes fate from collapse to inflation near $30\%$ instead of dying there, and is unmeasurably slow by $81\%$.}}{6}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:curve}{{4}{6}{One rate, two fates: the measured rate $1/\tau $ (left axis; $\tau $ right) against the angular momentum as a fraction of its extremal bound. Filled circles: collapsing rungs, $\tau $ from the log-linear fit of the areal-radius deficit over the 0.2--1\% band. Filled triangles: inflating rungs, $\tau $ from $\ln |dR_A/dt|$ over the $+0.2$--1\% growth band (the same fit on a pure exponential). Open circle: the stable 0.9c. Dashed: the fit $a-b\,(J/A)^2$ through both branches, which reaches zero at $42\%$. Open diamonds: the second-order rates of Refs.~\cite {azad2023,azad2024} at $C=1$; dotted rules: their conjectured end of the instability (${\approx }30\%$) and the zero of their second-order rate ($33\%$). The outcome: the mode slows with spin, changes fate from collapse to inflation near $30\%$ instead of dying there, and is unmeasurably slow by $81\%$}{figure.4}{}}
