\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Stability of the 0.9c rung over its triplet $N=128/192/256$ ($L=128$; finest $\Delta x$ in each panel title), to $t=150$. (a)--(h)~Constraint norms per level with the same second-/fourth-order brackets as Fig.~\ref {fig:conv02}: every level converges with resolution and nothing breaks out over the window. (i)~The equatorial throat radius holds the stationary value, its offset falling with resolution. (j)~The areal throat radius drifts by $\le 7\times 10^{-5}$ over the full window. (k)~The $(2,0)$ extraction at $R=18$, relative to its $t=0$ read-off: fluctuations at the $10^{-4}$ level, no burst. (l)~The far-side puncture lapse falls smoothly at all three resolutions (the gauge, not the geometry). The outcome: the 0.9c throat is stable on its window at every resolution---no growing radius, no constraint breakout, no wave.}}{10}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conv09}{{7}{10}{Stability of the 0.9c rung over its triplet $N=128/192/256$ ($L=128$; finest $\Delta x$ in each panel title), to $t=150$. (a)--(h)~Constraint norms per level with the same second-/fourth-order brackets as Fig.~\ref {fig:conv02}: every level converges with resolution and nothing breaks out over the window. (i)~The equatorial throat radius holds the stationary value, its offset falling with resolution. (j)~The areal throat radius drifts by $\le 7\times 10^{-5}$ over the full window. (k)~The $(2,0)$ extraction at $R=18$, relative to its $t=0$ read-off: fluctuations at the $10^{-4}$ level, no burst. (l)~The far-side puncture lapse falls smoothly at all three resolutions (the gauge, not the geometry). The outcome: the 0.9c throat is stable on its window at every resolution---no growing radius, no constraint breakout, no wave}{figure.7}{}}
